{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>By command of YHWH [it shall be visited].</b> This visitation shall be upon the besiegers." "<b>With storm.</b> By hailstones." "<b>With earthquake.</b> In the land." "<b>[And a voice, etc.].</b> And with a great voice in whirlwind and storm, with a flame of fire — the meaning concerns the going forth of the angel upon the camp of Assyria to destroy it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {3 "Ibn Ezra reads ברעם (\"with storm\") as referring to hailstones (גלגל, literally 'hail' per biblical usage e.g. Isaiah 28:17, 28:2) and ברעש as earthquake in the land; the bracketed lemma [וקול וגו'] and bracketed [תפקד] in comment 0 indicate reconstructed lemma headings from the manuscript tradition."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:48.120115777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}